response:
**Gates before launch.** I assumed three things that the situation does not state. The configs live in spe/evals/configs/B/ and spe/evals/configs/C2/, each with prompt.md and tools.json. Trial outputs go to spe/evals/runs/r04/. grade.py takes `--answers` and `--runs`. First I confirm that pwd, the git remote, and the branch match this repo. Next I run `git diff --quiet HEAD -- spe/predictions/r04.yaml spe/plans/r04.md`. That shows the predictions and the plan are still exactly as committed, so they are fixed before any data exists. Then I diff this script against spe/evals/harness/r03-workflow.js. The only differences should be the planned ones: the two configs, 50 tickets, 5 trials, the Opus judge, and the cap. I check grade.py in two ways. First I feed it a copy of answers.json as its own input, and it must score 100%. Then I feed it one file with a deliberately wrong label, and it must mark that row wrong. Next I launch with `smoke: true`, which runs 2 tickets once on each config and writes to spe/evals/runs/r04-smoke/. I use the smoke run and round 3's actual spend to set `estTrialUsd`, `estJudgeUsd`, and `estGradeUsd`. The full run is 500 trials plus 500 judge calls. If 500 x (trial + judge) plus grading comes to more than $40, I stop and ask you. I do not quietly cut trials. The script also enforces the cap. It reserves the estimated cost before each call, and it stops starting new trials when the next one would go over $40. The cap uses estimates because the script cannot see real billing. Last, I save the script as spe/evals/harness/r04-workflow.js and commit it locally. Then I launch.

```js
export const meta = {
  name: 'spe-r04-eval',
  description: 'SPE round 4. Configs B (12-line prompt, 6 tools) and C2 (12-line prompt, 3 tools + check_status). 50 tickets x 5 trials. Code grader on label.category and label.priority. Opus judge on reply tone. $40 cap.',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Preflight' },
    { title: 'Trials' },
    { title: 'Grade' },
    { title: 'Summary' },
  ],
};

const ROUND = 'r04';
const CONFIGS = ['B', 'C2'];
const N_TICKETS = 50;
const CAP_USD = 40;
const ANSWERS = 'spe/evals/tasks/answers.json';
const GRADER = 'spe/evals/graders/grade.py';
const JUDGE_RUBRIC = 'spe/evals/graders/judge.md';

// ---- Inputs. The script cannot read disk, so the launcher passes these in args.
const a = args ?? {};
if (!Array.isArray(a.tickets) || a.tickets.length !== N_TICKETS) {
  throw new Error(`args.tickets must list exactly ${N_TICKETS} ticket ids`);
}
for (const k of ['estTrialUsd', 'estJudgeUsd', 'estGradeUsd']) {
  if (!(typeof a[k] === 'number' && a[k] > 0)) {
    throw new Error(`args.${k} is required. Set it from r03 actual spend and the smoke run.`);
  }
}
const SMOKE = a.smoke === true;
const TICKETS = SMOKE ? a.tickets.slice(0, 2) : a.tickets;
const TRIALS = SMOKE ? 1 : 5;
const OUT = SMOKE ? `spe/evals/runs/${ROUND}-smoke` : `spe/evals/runs/${ROUND}`;
const MODEL = a.model ?? 'opus';   // system under test. Never Haiku by default.
const JUDGE_MODEL = 'opus';        // fixed by the approved plan

// ---- Budget. Reserve the estimate before each call. JS is single-threaded, so this check has no race.
let reserved = 0;
const skipped = [];
function reserve(usd) {
  if (reserved + usd > CAP_USD) return false;
  reserved += usd;
  return true;
}

// ---- Schemas
const PRE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['ok', 'checks'],
  properties: {
    ok: { type: 'boolean' },
    checks: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['name', 'pass', 'detail'],
        properties: { name: { type: 'string' }, pass: { type: 'boolean' }, detail: { type: 'string' } },
      },
    },
  },
};

const TRIAL_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['ok', 'path'],
  properties: {
    ok: { type: 'boolean' },
    path: { type: 'string' },
    category: { type: 'string' },
    priority: { type: 'string' },
    reply: { type: 'string' },
    error: { type: 'string' },
  },
};

const JUDGE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['score', 'pass', 'reason'],
  properties: { score: { type: 'number' }, pass: { type: 'boolean' }, reason: { type: 'string' } },
};

const GRADE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['ok', 'rows', 'missing'],
  properties: {
    ok: { type: 'boolean' },
    error: { type: 'string' },
    missing: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    rows: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['ticket', 'trial', 'category_ok', 'priority_ok'],
        properties: {
          ticket: { type: 'string' },
          trial: { type: 'integer' },
          category_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
          priority_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
        },
      },
    },
  },
};

// ---- Phase 1: preflight. Read-only checks. The run aborts if any check fails.
phase('Preflight');
reserve(a.estGradeUsd);                       // preflight agent
if (!reserve(a.estGradeUsd * CONFIGS.length)) // hold grading budget so trials cannot use it up
  throw new Error('Cap too small to grade');

const pre = await agent(
  `Preflight for SPE ${ROUND}${SMOKE ? ' (smoke)' : ''}. This is read-only. Do not edit, stage, or commit anything.
Run each check and report pass or fail with a one-line detail.
1. files: these files exist: ${GRADER}, ${JUDGE_RUBRIC}, ${ANSWERS}, spe/predictions/r04.yaml, spe/plans/r04.md.
2. answers: ${ANSWERS} holds exactly these ${N_TICKETS} ticket ids, and each has label.category and label.priority: ${JSON.stringify(a.tickets)}
3. grader: copy ${ANSWERS} into a temp dir outside the repo and run ${GRADER} on that copy as if it were model output. It must report 100% on both fields.
4. frozen: "git status --porcelain -- spe/predictions/r04.yaml spe/plans/r04.md" prints nothing.
5. configs: spe/evals/configs/B/prompt.md and spe/evals/configs/C2/prompt.md are each 12 lines. B/tools.json lists 6 tools. C2/tools.json lists 4 tools, and one of them is check_status.
6. clean_out: ${OUT} does not exist or is empty.
Set ok to true only if every check passes.`,
  { label: 'preflight', phase: 'Preflight', model: MODEL, schema: PRE_SCHEMA },
);
for (const c of pre.checks) log(`preflight ${c.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'} ${c.name}: ${c.detail}`);
if (!pre.ok) throw new Error('Preflight failed. Nothing was run.');

// ---- Phase 2: trials, then a blind judge for each reply.
// Order is trial, then ticket, then config. If the cap stops the run early, both configs keep equal coverage.
phase('Trials');
const items = [];
for (let t = 1; t <= TRIALS; t++)
  for (const id of TICKETS)
    for (const cfg of CONFIGS) items.push({ cfg, id, t });

const trialPrompt = ({ cfg, id, t }) =>
  `You are one eval trial for SPE ${ROUND}. Config ${cfg}, ticket ${id}, trial ${t}.
Read spe/evals/configs/${cfg}/prompt.md and follow it as your instructions.
Use only the tools listed in spe/evals/configs/${cfg}/tools.json.
Read the ticket from spe/evals/tasks/tickets/${id}.json.
Do not open ${ANSWERS}, anything under spe/evals/graders/, or any other trial's output.
Write {"ticket":"${id}","trial":${t},"config":"${cfg}","label":{"category":...,"priority":...},"reply":...} to ${OUT}/${cfg}/${id}.t${t}.json.
Return ok, the path, category, priority, and reply. If you cannot finish, set ok to false and explain in error.`;

// The judge sees the ticket and the reply only. It never sees the config name.
const judgePrompt = ({ id, out }) =>
  `Score the tone of one support reply. Use the rubric, scale, and pass rule in ${JUDGE_RUBRIC}, and follow them exactly.
Ticket: read spe/evals/tasks/tickets/${id}.json.
Reply to score:
<reply>
${out.reply}
</reply>
Judge tone only. Ignore whether the labels are right. Return score, pass, and a one-sentence reason.`;

let judgeSeq = 0;
const results = await pipeline(
  items,
  async (it) => {
    if (!reserve(a.estTrialUsd + a.estJudgeUsd)) {
      skipped.push(it);
      return { ...it, skipped: true };
    }
    try {
      const out = await agent(trialPrompt(it), {
        label: `${it.cfg}/${it.id}/t${it.t}`,
        phase: 'Trials',
        model: MODEL,
        schema: TRIAL_SCHEMA,
      });
      return { ...it, out };
    } catch (e) {
      return { ...it, out: { ok: false, path: '', error: String(e) } };
    }
  },
  async (r) => {
    if (r.skipped || !r.out?.ok || !r.out.reply) return r;
    try {
      const tone = await agent(judgePrompt(r), {
        label: `judge-${++judgeSeq}`,   // opaque label, no config name
        phase: 'Trials',
        model: JUDGE_MODEL,
        schema: JUDGE_SCHEMA,
      });
      return { ...r, tone };
    } catch (e) {
      return { ...r, toneError: String(e) };
    }
  },
);
log(`trials done. ran=${results.filter((r) => !r.skipped).length} skipped=${skipped.length} reserved=$${reserved.toFixed(2)}`);

// ---- Phase 3: code grading with grade.py, one call per config. The budget for this was reserved up front.
phase('Grade');
const grades = await parallel(
  CONFIGS.map((cfg) => () =>
    agent(
      `Grade SPE ${ROUND} config ${cfg}. Do not edit any file.
Run: python3 ${GRADER} --answers ${ANSWERS} --runs ${OUT}/${cfg}
If the flags differ, read "python3 ${GRADER} --help" and use the matching flags.
Report one row per output file with ticket, trial, category_ok, and priority_ok, exactly as grade.py computes them.
Do not regrade anything by hand. Expected files are ${TICKETS.length} tickets x ${TRIALS} trials. List any missing or unparseable ones in missing.`,
      { label: `grade-${cfg}`, phase: 'Grade', model: MODEL, schema: GRADE_SCHEMA },
    ),
  ),
);

// ---- Phase 4: summary. Pure computation. No agents.
phase('Summary');
const pct = (n, d) => (d ? Math.round((1000 * n) / d) / 10 : null);
const expected = TICKETS.length * TRIALS;

const summary = {};
CONFIGS.forEach((cfg, i) => {
  const g = grades[i];
  const rows = g.ok ? g.rows : [];
  // Missing outputs count as wrong, so the denominator is always the full expected count.
  const both = rows.filter((r) => r.category_ok && r.priority_ok).length;
  const byTicket = {};
  for (const r of rows) (byTicket[r.ticket] ??= []).push(r.category_ok && r.priority_ok);
  const passAllK = TICKETS.filter((id) => (byTicket[id] ?? []).length === TRIALS && byTicket[id].every(Boolean)).length;

  const mine = results.filter((r) => r.cfg === cfg);
  const toned = mine.filter((r) => r.tone);
  summary[cfg] = {
    expected,
    ran: mine.filter((r) => !r.skipped).length,
    skipped: mine.filter((r) => r.skipped).length,
    trialErrors: mine.filter((r) => !r.skipped && !r.out?.ok).length,
    gradeOk: g.ok,
    gradeError: g.error ?? null,
    missing: g.missing,
    categoryAccPct: pct(rows.filter((r) => r.category_ok).length, expected),
    priorityAccPct: pct(rows.filter((r) => r.priority_ok).length, expected),
    bothAccPct: pct(both, expected),
    passAll5TicketsPct: pct(passAllK, TICKETS.length),
    toneJudged: toned.length,
    toneMean: toned.length ? Math.round((100 * toned.reduce((s, r) => s + r.tone.score, 0)) / toned.length) / 100 : null,
    tonePassPct: pct(toned.filter((r) => r.tone.pass).length, toned.length),
    judgeErrors: mine.filter((r) => r.toneError).length,
  };
  log(`${cfg}: both=${summary[cfg].bothAccPct}% cat=${summary[cfg].categoryAccPct}% pri=${summary[cfg].priorityAccPct}% pass^5=${summary[cfg].passAll5TicketsPct}% tonePass=${summary[cfg].tonePassPct}% skipped=${summary[cfg].skipped}`);
});

if (skipped.length) log(`WARNING: cap reached. ${skipped.length} trials were not run. Results are partial.`);

return {
  round: ROUND,
  smoke: SMOKE,
  outDir: OUT,
  capUsd: CAP_USD,
  reservedUsdEstimate: Math.round(reserved * 100) / 100,
  summary,
  trials: results.map((r) => ({
    cfg: r.cfg, ticket: r.id, trial: r.t,
    skipped: !!r.skipped, ok: !!r.out?.ok, error: r.out?.error ?? null,
    tone: r.tone ?? null,
  })),
};
```
